he grid.\n\n\n**Formulating Laser Rules**\n\nI've distilled a clear rule for these directional emissions. The 5-long bar emits a dashed laser, changing every other cell to its special color until the border. When the laser hits the border, that entire row or column becomes filled with the special color, but only the row or column where the border is located. I've observed that intersections of the border are reset to the initial cell value (0). I think I'm starting to get closer to a robust approach.\n\n\n",
